{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1579452551,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3NjAyMzM5MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4051#issuecomment-576023391"},"message":"We are working on supporting \"ephemeral\" clones for such scenarios. The idea is that with datasets that are prohibitively large, such that any copying is not a good idea, one can setup clones that share the \"master\" annex. The feature is already implemented, it just needs a bit of polish to get fit for a PR into master. The ETA for a PR is very soon (days rather than weeks) -- it would be fantastic to have it be tested broadly.\n\nPS: version 0.12.1 has been released. It would make sense to upgrade from rc6.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1579452551,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDM0MDIwMDE5OA=="},"target":"f156461bf6525a67a8f87ada19dbced9ee4d0778ce20144eb4d2111b3ef6bbbd","message":"We are working on supporting \"ephemeral\" clones for such scenarios. Ping @bpoldrack \n\nThe idea is that with datasets that are prohibitively large, such that any copying is not a good idea, one can setup clones that share the \"master\" annex. The feature is already implemented, it just needs a bit of polish to get fit for a PR into master. The ETA for a PR is very soon (days rather than weeks) -- it would be fantastic to have it be tested broadly.\n\nPS: version 0.12.1 has been released. It would make sense to upgrade from rc6.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1579452526,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI5NjEwMDkyNDg="},"added":["performance"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1579452526,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI5NjEwMDkyNDk="},"added":["severity-wishlist"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"a29d5859530e551c9c63051e6b73ecbf9e195803"},"timestamp":1579455432,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3NjAyNzYxNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4051#issuecomment-576027614"},"message":"Will upgrade in time. My data processing will finish in 15+ days, so I will update datalad with the new feature hopefully. This ephemeral idea though is new to me, and I would very much hope there is no mess-up of the master location. This is the reason why we use clones, i.e., researchers don't have access to write on the master location, and everything is vetted before being merged in the master location,","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"a29d5859530e551c9c63051e6b73ecbf9e195803"},"timestamp":1579455432,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDM0MDIwNjIwNg=="},"target":"65e0e628049731da6e284dfed957647f156040f987fcfd0130860e5ffead7fa3","message":"Will upgrade in time. My data processing will finish in 15+ days, so I will update datalad with the new feature hopefully. This ephemeral idea though is new to me, and I would very much hope there is no mess-up of the master location. This is the reason why we use clones, i.e., researchers don't have access to write on the master location, and everything is vetted before being merged in the master location.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1579467029,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3NjA0NTQ2Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4051#issuecomment-576045466"},"message":"Fwiw, if you use file system with cow (copy on write) support such as btrfs, copying data within filesystem could be done very efficiently and without wasting space. I would (will) have also checked if git annex move within clones on the same filesystem would just use mv command. \nBTW, for running fmriprep, do you use containers-run? We have ready to use containers etc in https://github.com/ReproNim/containers","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"a29d5859530e551c9c63051e6b73ecbf9e195803"},"timestamp":1579469144,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3NjA0OTAyNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4051#issuecomment-576049027"},"message":"@yarikoptic My storage array is, no btrfs unfortunately. I am using only datalad and not playing with git/annex just to be sure everything is done according to internal datalad procedures.\n\nI am using a singularity container for fmriprep, with the latest v1.5.5 from a few days ago. But I am not using it through `datalad containers-run` for two reasons:\n1. I need to run subjects in parallel with SGE job scheduler.\n2. I plan to create subdatasets for each subject to optimize the hierarchical organization of datasets for easy save/status/etc.\nSo, for now, I am producing the data, then will run `datalad create --force` to make the subdatasets, and after that merge changes in the master location.\n\nWhen posting the question here I was thinking that what I want to achieve can be done simply by\n1. `mv` the entire folder at the master location.\n2. Go to the parent dataset and add the entry in `.gitmodules` (I can even copy this entry from the clone location):\n```\n[submodule \"fmriprep-1.5.5\"]\n        path = fmriprep-1.5.5\n        url = ./fmriprep-1.5.5\n        datalad-id = 3f433c48-1398-11ea-98da-ecebb88942b0\n```\nWouldn't this be enough?","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"a29d5859530e551c9c63051e6b73ecbf9e195803"},"timestamp":1579469144,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDM0MDIzNjgwNw=="},"target":"35b2d25fa0c93c61d91eeb8182185bbbf19b724dc97d1d9005ec92a36c9f0e46","message":"@yarikoptic My storage array is not btrfs unfortunately. I am using only datalad and not playing with git/annex just to be sure everything is done according to internal datalad procedures.\n\nI am using a singularity container for fmriprep, with the latest v1.5.5 from a few days ago. But I am not using it through `datalad containers-run` for two reasons:\n1. I need to run subjects in parallel with SGE job scheduler.\n2. I plan to create subdatasets for each subject to optimize the hierarchical organization of datasets for easy save/status/etc.\nSo, for now, I am producing the data, then will run `datalad create --force` to make the subdatasets, and after that merge changes in the master location.\n\nWhen posting the question here I was thinking that what I want to achieve can be done simply by\n1. `mv` the entire folder at the master location.\n2. Go to the parent dataset and add the entry in `.gitmodules` (I can even copy this entry from the clone location):\n```\n[submodule \"fmriprep-1.5.5\"]\n        path = fmriprep-1.5.5\n        url = ./fmriprep-1.5.5\n        datalad-id = 3f433c48-1398-11ea-98da-ecebb88942b0\n```\nWouldn't this be enough?","files":null}]}